Base model
----------
Dodona's adapters are LoRA weights for Qwen2-Audio-7B-Instruct
(https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen2-Audio-7B-Instruct) by the Qwen team, Alibaba Cloud,
licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. The base model is not redistributed here;
it is downloaded from its own repository. Dodona changes it by adding two LoRA adapters
and a calibration layer on its answer probabilities.

Training data
-------------
The adapters and the calibration maps were fitted on the following corpora. None of their
audio, transcripts or labels is redistributed here.

AMI Meeting Corpus
  https://groups.inf.ed.ac.uk/ami/corpus/
  Licensed under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0).
  Carletta, J. et al. (2005). The AMI Meeting Corpus: A Pre-announcement.
  Machine Learning for Multimodal Interaction (MLMI).

CREMA-D (Crowd-sourced Emotional Multimodal Actors Dataset)
  https://github.com/CheyneyComputerScience/CREMA-D
  Contains information from CREMA-D, which is made available under the Open Database
  License (ODbL) v1.0; its contents under the Database Contents License (DbCL) v1.0.
  Cao, H. et al. (2014). CREMA-D: Crowd-sourced Emotional Multimodal Actors Dataset.
  IEEE Transactions on Affective Computing, 5(4), 377-390.

Common Voice (Scripted Speech 27.0 and Spontaneous Speech, English)
  https://commonvoice.mozilla.org
  Released under CC0 1.0 by the Mozilla Foundation.
  Ardila, R. et al. (2020). Common Voice: A Massively-Multilingual Speech Corpus. LREC.
